{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Aharon shall make atonement upon its horns once in the year.</b> One cannot say that blood was placed upon its horns only once a year, for it is written regarding the bull of the anointed priest — 'and he shall place some of the blood upon the horns of the altar of incense' — and likewise regarding the bull for an unwitting matter of the congregation. Rather, this is what it says: what the priest does <b>upon its horns once in the year</b> — namely, on Yom Kippur — that act is called 'atonement.' <b>Once in the year he shall make atonement upon it,</b> but on all the rest of the days of the year blood was not placed upon it (the altar top), only upon its horns. The passage of the order of Parashat Tetzaveh is complete."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The parenthetical '(שוה)' appears in the source; its exact referent is unclear. The final phrase 'שלימא סדרא דפרשת תצוה' is a colophon marking the end of the section."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:14.029578423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}